I carry the boxes across the hall from my old room.
Nina helps me.
There are not many boxes.
There are only books and clothes in them.
But two of them are very heavy.
Suddenly one of the boxes slips.
I catch it just in time.
We laugh.
We set the boxes by the door.
Now there are four boxes standing on the floor.
There are some clothes lying on one box.
"Pause!"
"I'll leave you to it," Nina says.
"Thank you so much for the help," I say.
Nina smiles and goes out into the hall.
She goes into her own flat right next door.
I close the door.
Now I am all alone in my new flat.
Now the flat is mine.
